# gsap-core

When you write GSAP code, use these conventions:

- Imports: `import { gsap } from "gsap"`. All plugins free since Webflow acquisition; no Club / `.npmrc` / auth token needed.
- Sequencing: `gsap.timeline()` with position parameter (`"+=0.5"`, `"<"`, labels). Avoid chained `delay`.
- Transforms: prefer GSAP aliases (`x`, `y`, `scale`, `rotation`, `xPercent`, `yPercent`) over raw CSS `transform` or layout (`top`, `left`, `width`).
- Opacity: prefer `autoAlpha` over `opacity` (also sets `visibility`).
- `gsap.from(autoAlpha:0)` on a CSS-hidden element animates 0 → 0 (no motion). Use `gsap.fromTo()` with explicit start state.
- Multiple `from()` / `fromTo()` on the same property of the same element: set `immediateRender: false` on later ones.
- Wrap every project in `gsap.matchMedia()` with at least `(prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference)` and `(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)` branches — paint end state in the reduced branch.

Pair with `motion-design-taste` for aesthetic direction before implementing.

For full reference: `skills/gsap-core/SKILL.md`.
